# Hosted Claude model — used by the PG Internals Expert, which
# single-handedly reasons out a realistic EXPLAIN plan AND draws the full
# diagram AND writes the slideshow (see PART 0 of PG_EXPERT_INSTRUCTION),
# so this defaults to an advanced/high-reasoning model. Requires an
# Anthropic API key: console.anthropic.com -> Settings -> API Keys ->
# Create Key. This is separate, pay-as-you-go API billing, NOT the same as
# a claude.ai / Claude Code subscription — that subscription does not
# grant API access.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8

# How long to let one Expert call run before giving up (seconds). One call
# now does a lot (plan reasoning + full pixel-precise diagram + a
# potentially 20-30+ slide slideshow) and can genuinely take a while —
# litellm's own default (600s) was measured actually timing out in
# testing, which silently fell back to an empty diagram with no visible
# error. NOTE: `google.genai.types.HttpOptions.timeout` is documented as
# milliseconds, but ADK passes it straight through to litellm's `timeout`
# kwarg with no ms->s conversion, and litellm's own `timeout` is in
# seconds — so this value is genuinely seconds, not milliseconds, despite
# what the underlying field's name/docs imply.
EXPERT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=900
